[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"410","stub":{"id":"410","section":"02. 1st Fork Bridge to Lower Piedra CG","altname":"First Box Canyon","river":"Piedra","difficulty":"IIItoIVplus","states":["USA-COL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"309","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112637","location":{"latitude":"37.3530731201172","longitude":"-107.324592590332"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117923","location":{"latitude":"37.2423400878906","longitude":"-107.342651367188"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"10","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"100270909","title":null,"post_date":"2008-03-12 04:00:00+00","detail":"On 3/12 the USFS notified AW that a bridge had fallen in the Piedra. Check out: http://www.americanwhitewater.org/events/info/piedra\\_poster.pdf for more information","user":{"name":"Ben VanCamp"}}],"photos":[{"id":"7580","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7190","description":"Decent line at Mudslide.   Entering the top rapid from lft to rt with about 1:00 angle, punching the curler and finishing with a 5 foot boof against the rt wall or rt side of the pillow rock at the bottom.","caption":"Line @ Mudslide","poi_name":"Mudslide Rapid","subject":"Brian Brown","author":"RBone","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7580","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7580"}},{"id":"7577","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7190","description":"Cold Water!","caption":"Run-out-Eye of the Needle","poi_name":"Eye of the Needle Rapid","subject":"Granite-Granny","author":"RBone","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7577","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7577"}},{"id":"7581","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7190","description":"","caption":"Left Line-Eye of the Needle","poi_name":"Eye of the Needle Rapid","subject":"Andy-Park City","author":"R","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7581","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7581"}},{"id":"1592","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1650","description":"","caption":"First Box Canyon, Piedra River","poi_name":"First Box","subject":"Craig Blakemore","author":"Mark Blakemore","poi_id":"107037","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1592","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1592"}},{"id":"814","ext":"bmp","post_id":"1650","description":"","caption":"First Box Canyon, Piedra River","poi_name":"First Box","subject":"Craig Blakemore","author":"Mark Blakemore","poi_id":"107037","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/814","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/814"}},{"id":"11880","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8860","description":"Yeah, you want to avoid that hole!","caption":"1st Mudslide, High Water","poi_name":"1st Mudslide","subject":"Randy Jackson","author":"Jack Zwaan","poi_id":"107038","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11880","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11880"}},{"id":"890772","ext":"jpg","post_id":"894710","description":null,"caption":"Drew Althage","poi_name":"First Mudslide","subject":null,"author":"Ty Skoe","poi_id":"107037","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890772","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890772"}},{"id":"7574","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7190","description":"This is the large rock in the middle of the drop that all the current flows into. There is a breaking curler that pushes from rt to left at the bottom of the drop which wants to push you dirctly into this large rock. I punched the curler with too much lft to rt angle  and ended up being flushed directly into the pillow rock but was luckily pushed rt after 2 good backstrokes, flipping, and being held breifly.  Left of the large rock is a nasty hole that would be difficult to get a rope to or any immediate rescue from.\r\nIMO this rapid is a mandatory scout on your first run.    ","caption":"Pillow Rock @ Mudslide","poi_name":"Mudslide","subject":"None","author":"R","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7574","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7574"}},{"id":"7571","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7190","description":"1st major rapid of the run.  Hero route is the boof on river rt over a large hole. Left line is straight forward punching the river-wide hole at the run-out.","caption":"Eye of the Needle Rapid-1st Box","poi_name":"Eye of the Needle Rapid","subject":"None","author":"RBone","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7571","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7571"}},{"id":"7579","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7190","description":"This is what I look like when I screw-up a Class V line. Luckily I was completely un-injured. (See Pillow rock for explanation)","caption":"Wide-Eyed","poi_name":"Mudslide Rapid","subject":"Robert Bone","author":"Brian Brown","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7579","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7579"}},{"id":"7570","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7190","description":"Entering the 1st Box","caption":"First Box -Piedra","poi_name":"1st Box","subject":"Park City Boys","author":"RBone","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7570","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7570"}},{"id":"11881","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8860","description":"","caption":"Entrance to Eye of the Needle","poi_name":"Eye of The Needle","subject":"Nathan Klema","author":"Jack Zwaan","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11881","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11881"}},{"id":"11882","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8860","description":"","caption":"Nate Threading the Needle","poi_name":"Eye of The Needle","subject":"Nathan Klema","author":"Jack Zwaan","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11882","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11882"}},{"id":"890731","ext":"jpg","post_id":"894669","description":null,"caption":"John Huisjen","poi_name":"Put In","subject":null,"author":"Drew Althage","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890731","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890731"}},{"id":"890732","ext":"jpg","post_id":"894670","description":null,"caption":"Drew Althage","poi_name":"Eye of the Needle","subject":null,"author":"Daniel Kreykes","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890732","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890732"}},{"id":"890733","ext":"jpg","post_id":"894671","description":null,"caption":"Jeff Dean","poi_name":"Eye of the Needle","subject":null,"author":"Daniel Kreykes","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890733","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890733"}},{"id":"890734","ext":"jpg","post_id":"894672","description":null,"caption":"Daniel Kreykes","poi_name":"Eye of the Needle","subject":null,"author":"Daniel Kreykes","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890734","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890734"}},{"id":"890771","ext":"jpg","post_id":"894709","description":null,"caption":"Jeff Dean, Todd Henry","poi_name":"Eye of the Needle","subject":null,"author":"Drew Althage","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890771","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890771"}},{"id":"891131","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895040","description":null,"caption":null,"poi_name":"Second Mudslide (Eye of the Needle)","subject":null,"author":"Tim Brink","poi_id":"107038","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891131","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891131"}},{"id":"891132","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895041","description":null,"caption":null,"poi_name":"Second Mudslide (Eye of the Needle)","subject":null,"author":"Tim Brink","poi_id":"107038","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891132","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891132"}}],"detail":{"id":"410","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"This section of the Piedra is an excellent class IV to IV+ run. To reach the put in, drive up the first fork road just East of where highway 160 crosses the river. The takeout is up this road also, just before the road leaves the river. If the gate is closed, you will have to run the upper section as well and do the long shuttle thing.\n\nThis run changed due to the flooding of 2005, and now the 2nd mudslide rock has 'opened up' a bit to make it slightly easier. Always scout this and consider portage or lining on the right and watch for wood!","averageGradient":"0","maxGradient":"0","length":"9.1","correlations":[{"reachID":"410","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"400","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"3500"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"PIEDRA RIVER NEAR ARBOLES, CO.","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"09349800","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"309","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.18","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"37.08834204","longitude":"-107.3978428"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/09349800","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/09349800/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"309","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["112637","117923"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-107.32465845168541,37.352973411957976],[-107.32485041051734,37.35310020868724],[-107.3250430771837,37.35312207535384],[-107.32514447718353,37.35316547535376],[-107.32617887718192,37.35259827535464],[-107.32688801051415,37.352150408688715],[-107.32723301051362,37.351878875355794],[-107.32771901051291,37.351248808690116],[-107.32791307717923,37.35